---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import PracticeLink from './PracticeLink.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../lib/siteConfig';
import evolyssePoster from '../assets/photos/commercial-evolysse-poster.jpg';
import vanPromoPoster from '../assets/photos/commercial-van-promo-poster.jpg';
import billboardPoster from '../assets/photos/commercial-billboard-poster.jpg';
import j2Poster from '../assets/photos/commercial-j2-poster.jpg';
import teamPoster from '../assets/photos/commercial-team-poster.jpg';

/**
 * HOME VIDEO CAROUSEL — the cinematic noir stage (operator direction
 * 2026-08-14, DECISIONS same date: "the way Audi presents video").
 * Five films crossfade on a full-bleed black stage: no player
 * chrome, thin progress bars, and three small controls — pause, and
 * since 2026-09-30 Sound and captions (Amy's request, DECISIONS same
 * date).
 *
 * FACADE PATTERN (BUILD_SPEC §9; also the perf fix — measured): the
 * server renders ONLY poster images. Parser-instantiated <video>
 * elements cost ~1.5–2.3s of throttled style/layout on this page
 * (TBT 335ms median, perf 0.89 — the failing 2026-08-14 runs); the
 * script builds each <video> on demand instead, so the load trace
 * contains zero media elements and zero video bytes.
 *
 * The films (J2 cleared 2026-08-14; team cleared 2026-08-17; Evolysse
 * 2026-09-25; the promo and the billboard-day reel 2026-09-27 —
 * DECISIONS, each date):
 *  - commercial-evolysse — the Evolus-produced Evolysse spot
 *    (US-EVY-2600017), FIRST in the rotation (operator direction
 *    2026-09-25). OPERATOR OVERRIDE after the compliance flag, carried
 *    AS-IS: a results-comparison segment, the location's co-branding
 *    with its phone, QR code and microsite, and a spelling error on
 *    Amy's title card. It ran on dermal-fillers 2026-07-21 → 2026-08-21
 *    and was retired at the client's direction; this is its return.
 *    It starts muted like every film here. Since 2026-09-30 (operator
 *    direction) its voiceover — which carries the spoken risk statement
 *    its on-screen lines do not — plays when the Sound button is on;
 *    the caption file transcribes it, off by default like every track
 *    (operator decision after the flag). The one 16:9 film:
 *    the stage's `width: 100%` is what lets it present large. NEVER
 *    trim or crop it; plays at 1×.
 *  - commercial-van-promo — Amy's own Mobile Aesthetics promo, second
 *    in the rotation since 2026-09-27: her studio, then the black van
 *    and the location's other providers stepping out of it. OPERATOR
 *    OVERRIDES after the compliance flags: constraint 2's eighth
 *    exception (the other providers on camera, releases confirmed on
 *    file; the practice's web address printed on every frame and on
 *    the poster — display-only, never printed in site text) and
 *    constraint 3's eleventh pixel-level override (the studio
 *    segment's product cartons and its tray with printed slot labels).
 *    Its label and these comments name nobody and restate none of that
 *    packaging or labelling. 720px wide, so below the 2× sharpness rule
 *    at the stage's height cap (1.78×) — a recorded exception. Plays
 *    at 1×. Its SOUND, since 2026-09-30, is a further OPERATOR OVERRIDE
 *    after the flags: a re-worded pop song that names people and makes
 *    a promise this site's own copy may not. The caption file carries
 *    the sung words (operator decision — the one place they are
 *    written); the label and these comments still restate none of it.
 *  - commercial-billboard — Amy's own reel of the day her billboard
 *    went up and a delivery reached her studio, third since
 *    2026-09-27. OPERATOR OVERRIDE after the compliance flag, carried
 *    AS-IS (constraint 3): the billboard photo's headline and brand
 *    lockup, a wall poster titling a competitor brand this site never
 *    names, and the manufacturer's boxes; both people on camera besides
 *    Amy are released (operator, same date). No text from the
 *    billboard, the poster or the boxes is ever restated — label,
 *    captions, these comments. A 576px copy: below the 2× sharpness
 *    rule on tablets and desktops (1.42× at the height cap) — a
 *    recorded exception until Amy's original arrives. Plays at 1×.
 *    Its sound is a commercial song, start to finish (operator
 *    override of the music-licence position, 2026-09-30).
 *  - commercial-j2 — the Evolus co-op Jeuveau spot (US-JUV-2600126)
 *    carried AS-IS, manufacturer safety text intact. NEVER trim or crop
 *    it: object-fit stays `contain` so the burned-in safety screens
 *    render complete. Its sound is the manufacturer's music, with no
 *    voiceover. Its twin, commercial-j1, ran from 2026-08-14 until the
 *    promo replaced it on 2026-09-27.
 *  - commercial-team — the Mobile Aesthetics "Girl team" film.
 *    Constraint-2 OPERATOR OVERRIDE 2026-08-17 (it features the
 *    location's other providers; flag raised, override chosen);
 *    releases for the five team members confirmed on file. Plays
 *    at 1×. Its sound is the song its /about rendition has played
 *    since 2026-08-25 (the same 2026-09-30 music override).
 *  No film sets a rate now. The studio reel (commercial-studio, from
 *  2026-08-14 until the billboard-day reel replaced it on 2026-09-27)
 *  played at 0.5× (operator/Amy 2026-08-15, tuned across
 *  three reviews: 0.8 and 0.65 both still read too fast — slowed at the
 *  player via data-rate/playbackRate, the master untouched; 0.5 is also
 *  the practical floor — engines clamp below it). The knob stays for
 *  Amy's own films; the manufacturer films always play at 1× — their
 *  presentation is carried as-is.
 *  SOUND (2026-09-30, Amy's request — DECISIONS same date). Every
 *  rendition carries its film's own sound; each is the `video` name
 *  below, a new object beside the silent one it replaced (the picture
 *  stream is that file's, copied bit for bit). The films still START
 *  muted; the Sound button turns sound on for the film playing and
 *  every film after it. One plain volume offset per film (no
 *  compression, no limiting) brings them to a common level — figures
 *  in DECISIONS — and the promo alone has three, one per section of
 *  its own mix.
 *  CAPTIONS. Every built video carries a captions track (the axe
 *  video-caption rule audits rendered <video> elements; not
 *  `default`); the CC button shows it, as does a device with captions
 *  switched on. With sound, each file is faithful to the sound: the
 *  Evolysse file is its voiceover with its on-screen text; the Jeuveau
 *  file its on-screen text, safety information included, with a music
 *  note; the billboard-day reel and the team film carry bounded
 *  [Music] cues (a film-long cue would sit over the whole play); the
 *  promo's carries its sung words. A film with NO audio track would
 *  still ship a track with no cues (the 2026-09-20 rule). The ?v= on
 *  data-vtt is a cache-bust (the files serve with a one-day max-age)
 *  — bump it when a caption file changes.
 *  Since 2026-08-17 the .mp4 files serve from siteConfig.mediaBase
 *  (Blob behind the same Front Door) — data-file is absolute. The
 *  .vtt captions stay same-origin in public/media/ ON PURPOSE
 *  (in-repo compliance audit trail; same-origin tracks need no CORS,
 *  so the built <video> needs no crossorigin attribute).
 *
 * Behavior contract:
 *  - Nothing loads until the stage scrolls into view (mobile data +
 *    the / Lighthouse budgets never see a video byte), then the active
 *    slide autoplays muted and slides rotate on end.
 *  - prefers-reduced-motion (operator decision 2026-09-03, DECISIONS
 *    same date): the films still autoplay muted and rotate — they are
 *    content with a pause control (WCAG 2.2.2 pause/stop/hide is the
 *    toggle button) — and only the crossfade stands down (CSS: the
 *    switch becomes a cut). Before that date nothing autoplayed under
 *    the preference, which is what an Android phone with "Remove
 *    animations" on reported as "the carousel doesn't autoplay".
 *  - Phones: a refused play() (iOS Low Power Mode, battery/data modes)
 *    is retried inside the person's first touch or key press — a
 *    touch-scroll's touchend counts — and the built <video> carries the
 *    muted + playsinline ATTRIBUTES beside the properties (iOS quirk).
 *  - Progress bars are buttons (jump to a film); fills track playback.
 *  - Sound and CC are toggle buttons (aria-pressed). Sound stays on
 *    from film to film and when the stage scrolls away and back; it is
 *    never on at load and never stored (no cookie, no storage). A film
 *    the browser will not start with sound plays muted and the button
 *    shows off. A pause is left alone: turning sound on never starts a
 *    paused film. Details in public/js/video-carousel.js.
 * Contrast on noir (recorded pairs): pink-500 fill 5.95:1; bar track
 * and control borders paper@55% ≈ 5.3:1 (clears the 3:1 UI bar); a
 * pressed Sound or CC button is noir on pink-500, 5.95:1.
 */

const slides: {
  /** The film's name: its caption file is /media/<file>.vtt. */
  file: string;
  /** The object the player loads from the media origin (no extension). */
  video: string;
  label: string;
  poster: ImageMetadata;
  /** Playback rate — set ONLY on Amy's own films (the Evolus films'
   * presentation is carried as-is; leave them at the 1× default). */
  rate?: number;
}[] = [
  {
    file: 'commercial-evolysse',
    video: 'commercial-evolysse-sound',
    label: 'Evolysse commercial — Mobile Aesthetics with Evolus',
    poster: evolyssePoster,
  },
  {
    file: 'commercial-van-promo',
    video: 'commercial-van-promo-sound',
    label: "Mobile Aesthetics promo — Amy's medspa and the van",
    poster: vanPromoPoster,
  },
  {
    file: 'commercial-billboard',
    video: 'commercial-billboard-sound',
    label: "Billboard day and a delivery at Amy's medspa",
    poster: billboardPoster,
  },
  {
    file: 'commercial-j2',
    video: 'commercial-j2-sound',
    label: 'Jeuveau commercial — Mobile Aesthetics with Evolus',
    poster: j2Poster,
  },
  {
    file: 'commercial-team',
    video: 'commercial-team-sound',
    label: 'Girl team — Mobile Aesthetics',
    poster: teamPoster,
  },
];
---

{/* The section is NAMED by an explicit label since 2026-09-27, no longer
    by the heading's id: the heading now holds a link, and the link's
    hidden new-tab note would otherwise land in the region's name. Keep
    the label's words the same as the heading's. */}
<section class="vc surface" data-surface="noir" aria-label="Mobile Aesthetics. On screen.">
  <div class="vc-head">
    {/* Heading only, no eyebrow — operator/Amy 2026-08-15: this
        section deliberately drops the label+heading signature (fewest
        words on the cinematic stage). Renamed from "The studio. On
        screen." 2026-08-17 (operator) when the team film joined — the
        carousel now speaks for the whole practice.
        Since 2026-09-27 the practice's name is a LINK to the practice
        site (operator override of constraint 2 after the flag — every
        visible mention, this heading included by the operator's choice;
        DECISIONS same date). The site's first link inside a heading:
        the home motion layer raises a heading that holds a link WHOLE
        (public/js/home-motion.js, section 4), because a word split
        drops the underline and hides the link's name. */}
    <h2 class="heading-2" id="vc-heading"><PracticeLink>Mobile Aesthetics</PracticeLink>. On screen.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="vc-stage" data-vc-stage>
    {
      slides.map((s, i) => (
        <div
          class:list={['vc-slide', { 'is-active': i === 0 }]}
          data-file={`${siteConfig.mediaBase}/${s.video}.mp4`}
          data-vtt={`/media/${s.file}.vtt?v=4`}
          data-label={s.label}
          data-rate={s.rate}
        >
          <Image
            src={s.poster}
            alt=""
            widths={[480, 720]}
            sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 40rem"
            quality={55}
            loading="lazy"
            class="vc-poster"
          />
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="vc-ui">
    <div class="vc-bars">
      {
        slides.map((s, i) => (
          <button
            class="vc-bar"
            type="button"
            aria-current={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
            aria-label={`Play film ${i + 1} of ${slides.length}: ${s.label}`}
          >
            <span class="vc-track"><span class="vc-fill" /></span>
          </button>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <div class="vc-controls">
      <button class="vc-toggle" type="button" data-state="paused" aria-label="Play the films">
        <svg class="vc-ic-play" viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 1l9 5-9 5z" /></svg>
        <svg class="vc-ic-pause" viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 1h3v10H2zM7 1h3v10H7z" /></svg>
      </button>
      {/* Toggle buttons: the name stays put and aria-pressed carries the
          state. The CC button's name holds its two visible letters
          (WCAG 2.5.3, label in name). */}
      <button class="vc-sound" type="button" aria-pressed="false">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M2 6h3l4-3v10l-4-3H2z" />
          <path class="vc-ic-off" d="M11.5 6l3 4m0-4l-3 4" />
          <path class="vc-ic-on" d="M11 5.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 5m1.8-7a6 6 0 0 1 0 9" />
        </svg>
        <span>Sound</span>
      </button>
      <button class="vc-cc" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Captions (CC)">CC</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{/* Behavior lives in a STATIC same-origin file, not a component script:
  * the CSP (script-src 'self', no unsafe-inline) kills Astro-inlined
  * scripts on the real host, and globally forcing scripts external
  * (assetsInlineLimit: 0) un-inlined every page's CSS and regressed
  * LCP on the heaviest page. public/js/ is the scoped answer — CSS
  * inlining untouched, script external by construction. Keep the
  * carousel logic in public/js/video-carousel.js. */}
<script type="module" src="/js/video-carousel.js" is:inline></script>

<style>
  .vc {
    padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }
  .vc-head {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .vc-stage {
    position: relative;
    /* A DEFINITE width, so the height cap never narrows the stage. With
     * an auto width, max-height transfers through the 4:5 ratio and the
     * stage shrank to a 4:5 box on wide screens (486×608 at 1280×800),
     * which played the 16:9 Evolysse film at 486×274. At 100% the box
     * stays full-width once the cap binds (1152×608 there → the film at
     * 1081×608), and every portrait film renders at exactly its old
     * size — measured at five viewports, DECISIONS 2026-09-25. */
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    /* Hug the 4:5 films on phones (no dead bands); the height cap takes
     * over on wide screens, where black space beside the portrait film
     * is the look. The 9:16 reel contains inside either way. */
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    max-height: min(76vh, 720px);
  }
  .vc-slide {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.7s ease;
  }
  .vc-slide.is-active {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  /* The poster underlies the JS-built <video> (which lacks the style
   * scope attribute — hence :global). NEVER cover: the films' safety
   * screens must render complete. */
  .vc-slide :global(img),
  .vc-slide :global(video) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
  }
  /* Two groups, the bars and the controls, side by side where they fit
   * and on two rows where they do not (every phone: see the bars
   * comment below). */
  .vc-ui {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .vc-controls {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .vc-bars {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .vc-bar {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 64px;
    height: 32px; /* ≥24px target (WCAG 2.2) */
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  /* Five bars at 64px + four 8px gaps = 352px — wider than a 390px
   * phone's 342px content box (and the 344px fold cover's 296px). 40px
   * bars make the group 232px; the 40×32 button stays above the 24px
   * WCAG target. (Four films ran 48px bars, 2026-08-17.) Since
   * 2026-09-30 the controls are their own group (three buttons, 213px
   * as measured) and wrap under the bars wherever the two do not fit
   * one row: every phone, and windows 601–632px wide, where the bars
   * are already at 64px. So the bars no longer share their row on a
   * phone, and a sixth film's bars (280px) would fit the fold cover
   * too. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .vc-bar {
      width: 40px;
    }
  }
  .vc-track {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 2px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ng-paper) 55%, transparent);
  }
  .vc-bar[aria-current='true'] .vc-track {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ng-paper) 78%, transparent);
  }
  .vc-fill {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--ng-pink-500);
    transform: scaleX(0);
    transform-origin: left;
  }
  .vc-toggle,
  .vc-sound,
  .vc-cc {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ng-paper) 55%, transparent);
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ng-paper);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .vc-toggle svg {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  /* The label type is the eyebrow's (13px, 600, tracked capitals) in the
   * control's own color. The right padding is smaller by the tracking
   * the last letter carries, so the word sits centered. */
  .vc-sound,
  .vc-cc {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .vc-sound {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0 calc(0.875rem - 0.18em) 0 0.875rem;
  }
  .vc-cc {
    padding: 0 0 0 0.18em;
  }
  .vc-sound svg {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  .vc-sound .vc-ic-off,
  .vc-sound .vc-ic-on {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .vc-sound[aria-pressed='false'] .vc-ic-on,
  .vc-sound[aria-pressed='true'] .vc-ic-off {
    display: none;
  }
  /* On: noir on pink-500 (5.95:1). */
  .vc-sound[aria-pressed='true'],
  .vc-cc[aria-pressed='true'] {
    border-color: var(--ng-pink-500);
    background: var(--ng-pink-500);
    color: var(--ng-noir);
  }
  .vc-toggle[data-state='paused'] .vc-ic-pause {
    display: none;
  }
  .vc-toggle[data-state='playing'] .vc-ic-play {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .vc-slide {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
